  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "`floor(shares * (NAV + 1) / (total_shares + 10^6))`, NAV from the upstream or `LastNav`.\\nTotal and a pure read: no storage write, no TTL bump, and no revert on any upstream\\nfailure. Reverts only on an uninitialised contract.",
      "name": "balance",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "from",
          "type_": "address"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "i128",
            "error_type": {
              "udt": {
                "name": "StrategyError"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Pulls `amount` from the allowlisted `from`, forwards it to the upstream and mints floor\\nshares on the measured NAV delta (not on `amount`), so the upstream's rounding is borne by\\nthe depositor. Refused with `NotAuthorized` while deposits are paused, before any upstream\\ncall.",
      "name": "deposit",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "amount",
          "type_": "i128"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "from",
          "type_": "address"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "i128",
            "error_type": {
              "udt": {
                "name": "StrategyError"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Keeper-only (dual check). Three steps:\\n1. If `data` is given and a reward distributor is set, claims the strategy's Merkl reward.\\n`data` is the cumulative amount (16 bytes big-endian) followed by the proof siblings\\n(32 bytes each); any other shape is `InvalidArgument`. The user and token of the claim\\nare always the strategy and its asset.\\n2. Deposits every idle unit of the asset upstream for the current holders: NAV rises, no\\nstrategy shares are minted. Skipped while fewer than `MIN_SWEEP_SHARES` strategy shares\\nare outstanding (nobody, or dust, holds the strategy): the asset stays idle.\\n3. Writes the counted upstream shares down to what the strategy's address really holds,\\nif that is less (never up: shares sent in by others stay uncounted), refreshes\\n`LastNav` when the read succeeds and emits the event with the swept amount.\\n\\nA claim the distributor refuses, a deposit the upstream refuses and a failed read do not\\nrevert it. It does fail on malformed `data`, on an upstream mint report that overflows\\nthe count",
      "name": "harvest",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "from",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "data",
          "type_": {
            "option": {
              "value_type": "bytes"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "void",
            "error_type": {
              "udt": {
                "name": "StrategyError"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Pays `amount` to `to` straight from the upstream. Never allowlist-gated. Needs a live NAV\\nread (`ExternalError` otherwise). Burns ceil shares on `max(amount, value of the upstream\\nshares the exit burned)`, so an upstream exit cost or rounding is paid by the leaver.\\nFails `InsufficientBalance` (nothing moved) above the vault's balance or when the exit\\ncosts more shares than the vault holds (except a one-unit round-up on an exit of the whole\\nposted balance, which takes all the vault's shares); an upstream refusal, including an exit above the\\nupstream's instant liquidity, is `ExternalError`. Any failure reverts everything.",
      "name": "withdraw",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "amount",
          "type_": "i128"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "from",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "to",
          "type_": "address"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "i128",
            "error_type": {
              "udt": {
                "name": "StrategyError"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
